<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Cumulative frequencies and plotting an ogive</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The table shows the [[if test="is(w=5)"]]masses, in kg (to the nearest kg), of \({@n@}\) sheep at Kajiado market[[else]]times, in minutes (to the nearest minute), that \({@n@}\) learners spent on homework one evening[[/if]].</p><p>(a) Complete the cumulative frequency column.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(w=5)"]]Mass (kg)[[else]]Time (minutes)[[/if]]</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (\(f\))</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Cumulative frequency (cf)</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[1]@}–{@hi[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[input:c1]] [[validation:c1]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[2]@}–{@hi[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[input:c2]] [[validation:c2]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[3]@}–{@hi[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[input:c3]] [[validation:c3]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[4]@}–{@hi[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[input:c4]] [[validation:c4]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[5]@}–{@hi[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[input:c5]] [[validation:c5]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[6]@}–{@hi[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[input:c6]] [[validation:c6]]</td></tr></table><div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) A cumulative frequency curve is drawn for these data.</p><div>The curve starts at the point \(\big(\) [[input:ans7]] \(,\ 0\big)\). [[validation:ans7]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) At what value of \(x\) is the cumulative frequency for the class {@lo[j]@}–{@hi[j]@} plotted?</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans8]] [[validation:ans8]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The cumulative frequency at an upper class boundary counts every value below that boundary. Each cumulative frequency is a running total: add each frequency to the one above it. The last one is the total, \({@n@}\).</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">\(f\)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">cf</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Upper class boundary</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[1]@}–{@hi[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[1]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@exd(ucb[1])@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[2]@}–{@hi[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[2]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@exd(ucb[2])@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[3]@}–{@hi[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[3]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@exd(ucb[3])@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[4]@}–{@hi[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[4]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@exd(ucb[4])@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[5]@}–{@hi[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[5]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@exd(ucb[5])@}</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@lo[6]@}–{@hi[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@f[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@cf[6]@}</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">{@exd(ucb[6])@}</td></tr></table><p>(b) The data are to the nearest whole number, so the first class really starts at the lower class boundary, \({@exd(lcb1)@}\). No values lie below it, so the curve starts at \(({@exd(lcb1)@},\ 0)\).</p><p>(c) Every value in {@lo[j]@}–{@hi[j]@} is below the upper class boundary, \({@exd(ucbj)@}\), so the cumulative frequency \({@cf[j]@}\) is plotted at \(x = {@exd(ucbj)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
